# Linux Disk Space Management

One of the most common issues in production Linux servers is running out of disk space.

I recently created a practical guide on managing disk space using interactive terminal tools and Cron-based automation.

My biggest takeaway is that disk cleanup shouldn't start when the server is already full. Regular monitoring and automation can prevent many production issues before they happen.

**Monitor → Analyze → Manage → Clean → Automate**

